Episode: jinglin-ai-pulse: the boundary left the model - Nvidia ships agent containment in silicon on the premise that the guardrail belongs outside the weights, Sonnet 5.5's in-model cyber safeguard refuses legitimate security work, AMD buys World Labs for $8.2B to get closer to the hardware, and Jensen Huang told Ezra Klein five days earlier that labs which cannot contain their experiments should be shut down
